WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.570
Mato Grosso, Brazil: where tropical
rainforest meets the farming frontier.

2
00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:11.630
In 2025, China imported 111.8
million tonnes of soybeans,

3
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:14.810
82.3 million of them from Brazil.

4
00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:21.250
In the Brazilian Amazon, soybean area grew
from 0.4 to 4.6 million hectares between

5
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.490
2000 and 2019.

6
00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:28.370
One study found Mato Grosso had Brazil's
highest deforestation rate and soybean

7
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.750
production since 2001.

8
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.370
So why might the farms
themselves end up paying for it?

9
00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:37.770
In this mission, you'll trace
how soy drives clearance,

10
00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:41.590
directly and by pushing
pasture into the forest.

11
00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:45.030
Then you'll sort the
impacts by time and scale.

12
00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:49.490
Your mission: explain why the farms
themselves might end up paying for clearing

13
00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:50.520
the forest.
